WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.677
The synth can send signals out, too.

2
00:00:02.677 --> 00:00:09.709
Every output starts switched off and quiet, with a soft start and a limiter, so nothing surprises your speakers or your modular.

3
00:00:10.168 --> 00:00:12.975
Sonification turns the picture into sound.

4
00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:18.991
A voice reads the raster: its brightness, motion and shape set pitch, loudness and filter.

5
00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:21.963
Each voice parameter has a source and a curve.

6
00:00:21.963 --> 00:00:26.129
Pick Graph Node, and a Sonify node in the graph can play the voice directly.

7
00:00:26.594 --> 00:00:29.332
Master volume starts at minus eighteen decibels.

8
00:00:29.332 --> 00:00:35.835
Test Tone checks your levels, and Sonification mutes itself whenever a microphone is listening, to avoid feedback.

9
00:00:36.294 --> 00:00:41.203
CV Out sends control voltage to a modular through a DC-coupled interface.

10
00:00:41.203 --> 00:00:47.996
Add an output and choose its type: continuous CV, gate, trigger, clock, or one volt per octave pitch.

11
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:55.926
Its source can be a modulation slot, a graph node, any parameter, the Pattern Generator, MIDI notes, or the tempo clock.

12
00:00:56.382 --> 00:01:01.072
And MIDI Clock Out, in the MIDI section, sends the tempo to drum machines and DAWs.

13
00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:06.268
Inputs and outputs together make the synth one module in a bigger system.

14
00:01:06.268 --> 00:01:07.567
Next: stereo and 3D.
